Database Design

PostgreSQL is used because it is a reliable relational database that supports structured data, constraints, indexes, and efficient SQL queries.

The employees table contains the following fields:

Field

Type

Description

id

SERIAL / Integer

Primary key

name

VARCHAR(150)

Employee name

email

VARCHAR(255)

Unique email address

department

VARCHAR(100)

Department name

designation

VARCHAR(150)

Employee designation

date_of_joining

DATE

Joining date


Setup Instructions

1. Clone the repository

git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>
cd Employee-Directory-Search-System

2. Setup the backend

cd backend
python -m venv venv

Activate the environment on Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate.bat

Install dependencies and start FastAPI:

pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload

API documentation: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

3. Configure PostgreSQL

Create a PostgreSQL database named employee_directory.

Create a backend/.env file:

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/employee_directory

Replace YOUR_PASSWORD with your PostgreSQL password.

4. Setup the frontend

Open another terminal:

cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev

Configure the backend URL in frontend/.env:

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000